  <layout>One page of text, one column of verse; running head with page number at top right; no margin notes.</layout>
  <page_number>54</page_number>
  <running_head>EPITAPHIA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">N OBITVM NOBILISSIMI</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="1">Herois Francisci Linouæi.</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Ioan. Iacomoti Carmen.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">
      <i>SI, Musa, longos Threicio licet Sonare plectus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>pectine, si lyra Mœrente concedis decoras</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Nobilium lachrymare mortes:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Nunc linque Pindi culmina: nunc leues</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Omitte risus, &amp; Charitum iocos.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Lugubre carmen, næniasque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Funereas, memoresque tristis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Effunde fletus. Occidit, occidit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Heul gentis ingens Francigenæ decus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Noxius Heros. Hunc cruenti</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Vis rapuit truculenta Martis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Hunc luctuoso perdidit impotens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Bellona tandem funere, patriam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Seruare dum tendit ruentem:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Dum Validis metuendus hostes</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Propulsat armis: &amp; Lotharingicos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Fastus retundit fortis, &amp; impias</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Rebellione, &amp; sceleftis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Fœderibus sociata tela:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Aut semimaurae signa Tyrannidis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Infesta frangens, non finit impiger</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Ignota crudeles Iberos</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Several words are set in a mixed, partly italic and long-s-like face; "Heul gentis" likely "Heroum gentis" and "Rebellione," / "sceleftis" (scelestis) uncertain; "Threicio" and "Infesta" read with some doubt. Verse lines are set as printed; the first paragraph is one stanza-block.</notes>
</page>
